
*******************************************************************************
redirect(filename<,'w'>)  - redirect text output to a file
*******************************************************************************

The redirect command will redirect text output from Vnmrbg to the
file specified by its first argument. The default is to append text
to the named file. If an optional second argument of 'w' is given,
the file will first be truncated. If a macro calls redirect from an
automation run, redirect is ignored. This is because automation
already redirects output to the acqlog file.

This is the equivalent of redirecting Vnmrbg output called
in a shell command by using the bash script >> or > tokens.

shell('Vnmrbg -mback -n1 "doSomething" >> logfile)
shell('Vnmrbg -mback -n1 "redirect(logfile) doSomething")

shell('Vnmrbg -mback -n1 "doSomething" > logfile)
shell('Vnmrbg -mback -n1 "redirect(logfile,'w') doSomething")
